id: pm-0sx3kz
title: "GH-720: diagnose unbuilt GitHub extension sources and recommend resolvable npm artifacts"
description: "GitHub extension installation copies a source tree without building it, then reports only a missing manifest entry when TypeScript repositories omit committed dist output. Detect this source-shape mismatch, explain that GitHub installs are source copies, recommend the exact npm package command when safely derivable, document author expectations, and retain fail-closed source integrity."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T00:58:27.183Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T07:24:52.258Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T07:24:49.503Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "A GitHub source with a missing manifest entry reports the copy-without-build cause without executing untrusted package scripts; When package metadata identifies a published package, remediation includes the exact npm source command; otherwise it recommends a locally built path; Extension author and install documentation distinguish GitHub source trees from built npm artifacts; Temporary-repository acceptance covers missing dist, committed dist, npm fallback, and bounded error output"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: GitHub source installs distinguish missing copied builds from invalid package entries and provide safe recovery guidance.
expected_result: A GitHub extension repository without built output fails with a source-specific actionable diagnostic.
actual_result: Validation emits github_source_entry_unbuilt with npm/local recovery while preserving generic diagnostics for other source kinds.
